<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia scraps monopoly on raw sugar imports.</title>
<headline>Indonesia scraps monopoly on raw sugar imports.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia on Monday announced that sugar producers could import raw sugar, dismantling the monopoly held by state commodities regulator BULOG.</p>
<p>Industry and Trade Minister Tunky Ariwibowo said the move was part of the country's latest package of economic deregulation measures.</p>
</text>
